{"schemaVersion":1,"release":"20261117-rep1","sourceHashNormalization":"utf8-lf-v1","scope":"Optional finite representation-law and common-basis workshop in two existing foundations lessons.","counts":{"indexedLessons":197,"optionalEdges":259,"newLessonIds":0,"newGraphEdges":0,"placements":2,"realAPIReferences":5,"supportedIntegerPoints":25,"groupElements":8,"orderedPairsPerFamily":64,"families":4,"stages":5,"newLocaleFiles":3,"independentPythonTests":8,"exactCorrectnessChecksPerReply":11,"extractedSourceNodeBuilders":20},"contract":{"action":"representation_actions","input":"Exactly point: two strict integers in [-2,2]. Manual calculation returns all four families and all64 pairs for that probe.","labels":"C4v planar action and fixed-z mirror embedding, ordered E,R,R2,R3,M,RM,R2M,R3M. Normal form R^k M agrees with the earlier composition workshop.","algebra":"For every family and pair, Python returns D(g)D(h),D(gh),their difference, chronological h-then-g frames, and both unit-basis images. Local selectors browse, never calculate scientific results.","passive":"One common S transforms every matrix and every coordinate; returned reconstruction identities prove the physical action is unchanged.","counterexample":"Changing only R preserves individual orthogonality,traces and even the matrix-coefficient Gram, but fails18/64 products. It is an inconsistent matrix collection, not a representation.","repeated":"All elements mapping to I2 form a legitimate nonfaithful representation on an auxiliary space. Repetition alone does not invalidate a representation and is not the geometric action on xy arrows.","diagonalization":"Two real reflections each diagonalize separately, but have a nonzero commutator and no common diagonal basis. A quarter rotation diagonalizes over C, not R.","lifecycle":"Only opening a native disclosure imports the optional interface. Inputs, local choices, predictions, notes, disclosures and complete results have per-lesson memory and independent export; task-scoped cancellation protects newer work."},"verification":["Five complete real API references, with independent integer/rational checks across all25 supported points and every ordered product.","Production renderer and actual host tests distinguish intentional counterexample failures from calculation errors, preserve old lesson/quiz/experiment state and check asynchronous cleanup.","Actual Worker loader retains isolated standard-library dependencies and unchanged earlier water/composition dependency plans.","Original historical fixture builders are genuinely recomputed before source identities change; global bilingual and extracted-source checks remain separate."],"boundaries":["A fixed eight-element teaching model and bounded integer probe input; not a general representation classifier.","Mixed and abstract-trivial coordinate ledgers do not describe the same physical xy rotations as the original action.","Character orthogonality assumes a representation; a formal norm does not independently certify the multiplication law or infer protected levels.","Exact examples and prediction feedback do not establish measured learning gains or whole-curriculum completeness."],"files":{".github/workflows/pages.yml":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":1993,"sha256":"431341c29e709078173b19125090b627cdf0d815a58a036ba28411693eddbe9d"},"GOAL-ROADMAP.md":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":84720,"sha256":"ac2689b999923c0aa25d2cf576d299b92a268f95aeb21d1f440425d28df29c84"},"dist/app.js":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":105966,"sha256":"2d1a2406afa3e961df56481bb9f908ddd91f9522acca850adc494125a0cee85e"},"dist/classroom-ui.js":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":32822,"sha256":"38beee59e6202dc40d5b9c6740268001df3f1b9c1734eb31fc6ee7560ecb9d16"},"dist/composition-ui.js":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":27832,"sha256":"df67d403b7845c1d8f86678a29bdd288e96c8642e00f7e9bf781404cac1a61d8"},"dist/data/pointgroup-lessons.json":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":35682,"sha2